# react-wagmi example: environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and uncomment what you need, then restart the dev server.
#
# Nothing here is required. With an empty .env.local the app runs on Sepolia (through the
# public testnet relayer) and on the cleartext dev chains, with public RPC endpoints.
#
# The sections are in order of how likely you are to need them:
#   1. Mainnet           needed for Ethereum or Polygon mainnet
#   2. Vaults            needed for the Vaults tab
#   3. Wallet connection optional
#   4. Overrides         optional: other relayers and RPC endpoints
#   5. Hosting           optional, only for a public deployment
#   6. Custom Zama env   advanced, only for another protocol deployment on Sepolia
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are built into the page and visible to anyone using it. The others
# (relayer URLs and API keys) stay on the server and never reach the browser.

# ─── 1. Mainnet ───────────────────────────────────────── needed for Ethereum or Polygon ───
#
# A mainnet network stays hidden until its relayer URL is set. The Zama relayer needs an API
# key (see README "Mainnet access"); a self-hosted relayer does not. Bare hosts, no /v2.

# MAINNET_RELAYER_URL=https://relayer.mainnet.zama.org
# MAINNET_RELAYER_API_KEY=
# POLYGON_RELAYER_URL=https://relayer.mainnet.zama.org
# POLYGON_RELAYER_API_KEY=

# ─── 2. Vaults ─────────────────────────────────────────────── needed for the Vaults tab ───
#
# The confidential vaults of each network: one depositBatcher:redeemBatcher pair per vault,
# comma-separated. The app reads everything else (tokens, names, rates) from the chain.
# A network with no vaults shows a setup hint; one with several shows a vault picker.
# Network keys: SEPOLIA, BNB_TESTNET, HOODI, ZENITH, MAINNET, POLYGON.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SEPOLIA_VAULTS=0xDeposit:0xRedeem
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_VAULTS=0xDeposit:0xRedeem,0xOtherDeposit:0xOtherRedeem

# ─── 3. Wallet connection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── optional ───
#
# Dynamic (https://app.dynamic.xyz) environment ID. When set, "Connect Wallet" opens a dialog
# with Dynamic's wallet catalogue: browser wallets and WalletConnect, which is how a Safe
# pairs from the Safe web app. Unset, the app uses the browser wallet only.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_DYNAMIC_ENVIRONMENT_ID=

# ─── 4. Overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── optional ───
#
# Another Sepolia relayer, for example a private one. Defaults to the public testnet relayer,
# which needs no key. Bare host, no /v2.

# SEPOLIA_RELAYER_URL=https://relayer.testnet.zama.org
# SEPOLIA_RELAYER_API_KEY=

# Another RPC endpoint per network. Each defaults to a public endpoint.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BNB_TESTNET_RPC_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HOODI_RPC_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZENITH_RPC_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POLYGON_RPC_URL=

# ─── 5. Hosting ──────────────────────────────────────────── optional, public deployment ───
#
# See README "Hosting". Nothing here is needed to run the app locally.

# Only offer and proxy these networks. Unset offers every network the server can serve,
# including the cleartext dev chains.
# ENABLED_NETWORKS=mainnet,sepolia

# Footer links. The commit falls back to Vercel's VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA; a fork sets its own
# repository.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COMMIT_SHA=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOURCE_REPO_URL=https://github.com/zama-ai/sdk

# ─── 6. Custom Zama environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────── advanced ───
#
# Another protocol deployment on Sepolia, for example a pre-release one. Adds a
# "Sepolia · Custom environment" option next to Sepolia in the picker, using the gateway,
# protocol contracts and registry below. With NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAMA_ENV=custom, every value is
# required except the relayer API key.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAMA_ENV=custom
# Its relayer (server-side only, bare host, no /v2). The option is hidden while the URL is unset.
# SEPOLIA_CUSTOM_RELAYER_URL=
# SEPOLIA_CUSTOM_RELAYER_API_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAMA_GATEWAY_CHAIN_ID=0
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAMA_ACL_ADDRESS=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAMA_KMS_VERIFIER_ADDRESS=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAMA_INPUT_VERIFIER_ADDRESS=0x...
# Gateway contracts, used for the EIP-712 signatures:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAMA_DECRYPTION_ADDRESS=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAMA_INPUT_VERIFICATION_ADDRESS=0x...
# The environment's wrapper registry (a ConfidentialTokenWrappersRegistry you deployed).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=0x...
